  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\n`about:srcdoc` urls currently [require storing the policy container in history](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#requires-storing-the-policy-container-in-history). That implies that history navigations to srcdoc iframes will be reload the policy container from history, instead of inheriting it from the parent. Yet the srcdoc content is not stored in history, but reloaded from the iframe `srcdoc` attribute.\n\nIn the edge case in which both the parent's policy container and the srcdoc attribute change while there is a history navigation, this can result in an inconsistency between the history policies and the srcdoc content.\n\nMaybe it makes more sense to always inherit the policy container from the parent for srcdoc iframes.",
